nodecode-kata is a rewrite of opeblow's opeblow/kata:

  https://github.com/opeblow/kata
  commit cc59b08f1bbeeb02524c060faac04edb34de0564
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 opeblow (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the record of tool calls (a `:tool` hook, in memory, arguments
masked by name and by shape), the miner (per-session runs, windows of 2..N
tool names counted across separate sessions, fragments dropped when a longer
window repeats at least as often), the template inference reduced to constants
and named parameters (the original also recovers data flow from an earlier
step's result), the compile/run/forget lifecycle with the routines in one JSON
file of the cell's own, and the operator surface (one tool, one `/kata` command
and one manual topic, where the original had a dashboard page served by a
FastAPI router). Left out, because Nodecode's own seams and one JSON file of
the cell's own do not need them: the FastAPI dashboard and its JavaScript
bundle; SQLite and the plugin's own migrations; leave-one-out scoring (the
rewrite reports a fit rate but does not refuse on it); the twelve validator
checks, so a routine whose steps share no value is compiled rather than
rejected; effect classification and the approval rule for side-effecting
routines; the token and time baseline measured from the host's request log;
and the redaction of results (results are clipped, not masked, and never leave
the image).
